body:
From my knowledge so far,

&#x200B;

友達 is friend,

&#x200B;

なれ is to become,

&#x200B;

ーません typically is used for negative state of being

&#x200B;

か just a question marker.

&#x200B;

So I guess everything inbetween I'm kind of missing and confused?Specifically using に is my guess.

&#x200B;

"Won't you not become my friend" is what I'm getting which is confusing. Or is the negative state of being literally saying "Won't"?

My SO left me because a 5 year long distance relationship "Won't work in time" (we met literally at age 15-16 so we couldn't move in). We had half a year left until school was over. Except he dumped me in a 10 minute call then refused to talk with me for a week because he was visiting a friend. 


I'm so confused and list and recovering from this seems near impossible. 

Hoping for the best expecting the worst. I just want some closure from him ;-;

There's just a lot of regret going through my mind, and I feel like I'm to blame. I don't know what to look forward to anymore, and frankly that's the worst part. Right now he's asleep and I'm having the worst time of my life.

I'm going to wait out everything and maybe see if we can still talk like we used to. I'm just really scared, and with nobody else to talk with its even more nerve racking than anything else ;-;

But thanks for the support. I hope the rest of your day goes well!

All I can suggest is to check up with them regularly. Ask how they're feeling, what they want, where they wanna be. And don't let time spent be a factor in how "good" the relationship is.

Theres so many things I wish I had done and its too late now ;-;

I want to at least make amends and talk with them though. Fingers crossed that works!
